---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout>
    <section>
        <div class="relative px-8 py-12 mx-auto md:px-12 lg:px-32 max-w-7xl lg:pb-24">
            <div class="text-center">
                <h1
                    class="text-5xl font-semibold font-display text-blue-950 sm:text-6xl text-balance w-3/4 mx-auto">
                    What is OnTrack? 
                </h1>
                

            </div>
            <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-left text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                <img src="/public/MATTERImages/OnTrackQuote.png" />
            <p>OnTrack is a unit management system designed specifically to support the OnTrack Education Framework in delivering truly student-centred learning experiences.
</p> 

 

<h2>OnTrack for Students</h2>

<p>In OnTrack, students complete tasks to learn content, develop skills, and evidence their learning. They submit tasks for feedback during the teaching period, and their assigned tutor views the work and leaves feedback. The student is able to submit the same task multiple times until it is judged acceptable.

“I really like that you can work according to your grade preference, unlike other units where you submit a heavy weight grade assessment and waiting ages to get results to see how far you have come along” 

“[I liked that the unit had a] straightforward structure and giving chances for improvement and better understanding of the tasks or the concepts via the feedback cycles” 

“OnTrack is a great website, and the ‘self-led’ grading system where results are not determined by confounding factors, but the exact amount of effort and time that a student wishes to dedicate to the unit” 

The OnTrack system gives students agency over their learning, enabling them to choose their target grade, adjust their due dates and see a burndown chart of their progress through the tasks.
</p>

<h2>OnTrack for Staff</h2>

<p>With OnTrack teaching staff can manage the content, sequence, and submission dates for learning tasks. 
Tutors can manage interactions with the students both online and in class.
Unit Leads can manage the work of all the teaching staff assigned to the unit.</p>

<p>“The platform and the pedagogy behind inform a very close student-educator relationship, constant communication and exchange on the learning journey”</p>

<p>“Students gain responsibility and autonomy in own work, everything is very transparent” </p>

<p>“I don’t see how we could run the same level of student feedback with any other system” </p>



<img src="/public/MATTERImages/OnTrack-StudentPlanner.png" />

<h2>OnTrack features</h2>

<h3>Personalised learning functions</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Presentation of tasks based on student’s target grade ✅ </li>
<li>Ability for student to self-select target grade ✅ </li></ul>

<h3>Feedback functions</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Granular task statuses supporting formative feedback ✅ </li>
<li>At-a-glance student dashboard ✅  </li>
 <li>Single-click for students to view tutor feedback ✅  </li>
 <li>Comments from staff ✅   </li>
 <li>Comments from students ✅   </li>
 <li>Comment chains ✅   </li>
 <li>Full markdown support ✅   </li>
 <li>Text and audio comments, with optional attachments ✅   </li>
 <li>Tutor inbox showing at-a-glance what needs feedback ✅  </li></ul>


<h3>Submission functions</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Submission of student work ✅  </li>
<li>Submission history ✅  </li>
<li>Automatic similarity detection using JPlag and Turnitin ✅ </li>
<li>Automated portfolio compilation ✅ </li></ul>

<h3>Unit management functions</h3>
<li>Automated marking ✅ </li>
<li>Built-in feedback moderation system ✅</li>
<li>Visualisation of individual student progress ✅ </li>
<li>Automatic rollover of content between semesters ✅</li>
<li>Single sign-on integration ✅</li>
<li>LMS integration ✅</li></ul>



        </div>
    </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
